929 0 obj
<</ActualText(External Consultant \(Client Facing\) \(March 2023 - March 2024\)\n1 Billion Technology\nOperated as the primary external-facing analytics consultant for the organisation, independently managing the full end-to-end analytics lifecycle across concurrent cl\
ient engagements from discovery and scoping through to production deployment.\nLed stakeholder discovery and requirements definition sessions directly with client leadership, translating ambiguous business objectives into structured analytics requirements\
, semantic model designs, and phased delivery plans without dedicated product or business analysis support.\nEstablished organisation-wide analytics engineering standards covering Power BI architecture, semantic modelling conventions, DAX patterns, and vi\
sualisations, adopted as the default delivery framework across client projects.\nDelivered scalable semantic data models and Power BI reporting suites across multiple concurrent client engagements, enabling executive and operational decision-making across\
 enterprise stakeholders and ensuring consistent reporting.)/K 10/P 926 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
930 0 obj
<</ActualText(Engineer - Analytics and Data Science \(April 2024 - July 2025\)\n1 Billion Technology\nReduced dashboard delivery cycles from 12 weeks to under 2 days through reusable semantic modelling patterns, standardised Figma design system, DAX optimisation, and \
streamlined development workflows, significantly improving development efficiency and stakeholder turnaround time.\nDelivered 200+ production Power BI reports across 7+ project workspaces, supporting hundreds of end users across multiple client organisati\
ons and enabling consistent enterprise reporting across business functions.\nDesigned and implemented a reusable Figma-based analytics design system adopted across client projects, standardising UI components, layouts, and visual hierarchy, improving cons\
istency, development speed, and stakeholder adoption of solutions.\nDesigned and optimised enterprise semantic data models across concurrent client engagements, improving query performance, scalability, and cross-report consistency, and establishing reusa\
ble modelling patterns adopted across the team.\nDesigned and delivered an internal HR analytics platform for executive leadership covering workforce planning, recruitment pipelines, account structures, and project allocation, which was later commercialis\
ed by the company as the foundation of a standalone HR SaaS product.\nDelivered executive-level business performance reporting solutions for a GCC-based tech-enabled Employer of Record \(EOR\) and business consultancy firm, consolidating operational and c\
ommercial metrics into unified leadership dashboards, replacing fragmented manual reporting processes and improving executive visibility.\nApplied NLP-based text similarity techniques to unstructured client requirement data, enabling identification and gr\
ouping of semantically related requirements across different categories to support downstream analysis and reporting use cases.\nContributed to Microsoft Fabric and Databricks \(PySpark\) data engineering initiatives by developing Bronze and Silver layer \
transformations within a medallion architecture, supporting downstream semantic modelling and enterprise reporting layers.)/K 9/P 925 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
931 0 obj
<</ActualText(Senior Software Engineer - Analytics and Data Science \(August 2025 - Present\)\n1 Billion Technology\nSole analytics owner for a UK-based Microsoft Dynamics 365 SaaS provider, scoping, modelling, and deploying the full analytics suite serving enterprise \
clients, translating high-level business discussions into production-ready analytical systems without a formal requirements process.\nArchitected and delivered analytical products across sales, operations, finance, and customer success functions, providin\
g stakeholders with a unified analytics hub for operational KPIs, survey intelligence, and ISV product performance used for day-to-day and executive decision-making.\nReplaced manual executive reporting workflows with near-real-time Power BI dashboards, d\
efining KPI frameworks, metric hierarchies, and reporting standards, significantly reducing reporting overhead and enabling faster business decision cycles.\nEvaluated and piloted Databricks AI/BI Genie as a conversational analytics layer over enterprise \
datasets, demonstrating natural-language business data exploration capabilities.\nDesigned AI-assisted narrative reporting proof-of-concepts using Power BI Copilot, improving the relevance and usability of generated analytical commentary through iterative\
 prompt and context engineering.\nPartnered on technology evaluation and adoption for the analytics practice, assessing and integrating Microsoft Fabric Lakehouse, Databricks, and Fabric AI capabilities into both client delivery workflows and internal eng\
ineering standards.)/K 8/P 924 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
932 0 obj
<</ActualText(EXPERIENCE)/K 7/P 923 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
933 0 obj
<</ActualText(Senior Software Engineer specialising in Analytics Engineering and Applied Data Science with 4+ years building production-grade intelligence systems for enterprise environments. Sole analytics owner for a UK-based Microsoft Dynamics 365 SaaS provider, del\
ivering 200+ reports across 7+ production workspaces and reducing dashboard delivery cycles by up to 75% through scalable data modelling and development practices. Expertise spans Power BI, Microsoft Fabric, Python, Databricks, machine learning, and graph\
-based intelligence systems, with a focus on transforming complex operational data into decision-ready systems for executive and business users. First Class Honours Gold Medal graduate from Coventry University \(4.0 GPA\) and four-time international data \
competition award recipient.)/K 6/P 922 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
934 0 obj
<</ActualText(SUMMARY)/K 5/P 921 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
935 0 obj
<</ActualText(Colombo, Sri Lanka \(Open to remote and international roles\))/K 4/P 920 0 R/Pg 946 0 R/S/Span>>
endobj
